course: dictionary
lesson: 10764
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, and the words around it tell you which meaning the writer wants. «A broken umbrella is useless.» Here useless means not able to do its job. A broken umbrella cannot keep you dry, so it is useless.
explain: «It's useless to argue.» Now useless means having no effect. Arguing will not change anything, so there is no point in doing it. Read the whole sentence before you decide what the word means.
explain: «I'm useless at drawing.» In this sentence useless is informal, and it means very bad at something. It is a common thing to say, but it is not a helpful one. Drawing gets better with practice, so keep trying.
explain: To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence. If «a broken umbrella is not able to do its job» still makes sense, you have chosen the right meaning. Useless is an adjective, so it can also be more useless or most useless.
fact: Useless means not useful, or not able to do its job.
fact: «It's useless to argue» means there is no point in arguing, because it will have no effect.
fact: «Useless at» is a phrase meaning very bad at something, as in «I'm useless at baking».
fact: One burned cake does not mean you are useless at baking forever. One bad result is not the whole story.
fact: «-less» means without, so useless means without use.
exercise: «A broken umbrella is useless.» What does useless mean here? | Full of colour | Very kind and helpful | *Not able to do its job | Brand new and shiny
exercise: «It's useless to argue.» What does useless mean in this sentence? | Very loud | Full of fun | *Having no effect | Very tired
exercise: Nadia says «I'm useless at drawing» means she can never draw anything. What is the best answer? | It means she has broken her pencil | *It is an informal way of saying she is very bad at drawing right now, and she can keep practising | It means drawing is useless for everyone | It means she is the best artist in the class
test: «Eyes are useless in darkness, so the fish lost them.» What does useless mean here? | *Having no use | Full of light | Slowly moving | Very dark
test: What does the ending -less mean in «useless»? | Again | More than | Full of | *Without
exam: Ali writes «My essay is useless, so I give up.» Why is giving up not a good idea? | Because useless means very good | Because the essay is always perfect | *Because one weak try does not mean he cannot improve, and teachers want him to keep trying | Because essays never need work
